resources.string:
"1. \"Caller identification\" is a service provided by HeyTap and its third-party partners that identifies and marks unknown phone numbers.

2. To provide you with this service, it needs to collect unknown numbers from incoming calls and access the internet so it can identify and mark the unknown phone numbers via the Internet. You may turn this service on or off anytime in \"Contacts - Settings - Caller identification\". After you turn off this service, unknown phone numbers will no longer be identified and marked for you via the internet. (HeyTap and its third-party partners will not disclose your personal information to any other companies, organizations, or individuals without your consent unless otherwise permitted by laws and regulations);

3. The number identification results provided by this service come from data provided by other users, information publicly available on the Internet, and data provided by third-party partners:
(1) Completely accurate identification results are not guaranteed by HeyTap and its third-party partners, who are only filtering the data by technical means and are doing their best to provide users with reliable results. Users still need to verify for themselves the authenticity, accuracy, validity, and security of these phone and SMS numbers;
(2) HeyTap and its third-party partners have provided error reporting and number re-marking features to help users report incorrect information."

